§ `Part III - Determination of disputes`

§§ `Division 3 - Retaliatory action taken by lessor`

§§§ `26A. Retaliatory action`

DECLARE `lessor action` HAS
    `the lessor gives the tenant a notice claiming the tenant has breached the residential tenancy agreement, other than by failing to pay rent, and requiring the tenant to remedy the breach` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor increases the rent payable under the residential tenancy agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor takes action to terminate the residential tenancy agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at the end of the current residential tenancy agreement, the lessor refuses to enter into a further residential tenancy agreement with the tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor is motivated to take the action, wholly or partly, by the matter arising` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN a IS A `lessor action`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessor takes action of a kind in section 26A(a)` IF
        a's `the lessor gives the tenant a notice claiming the tenant has breached the residential tenancy agreement, other than by failing to pay rent, and requiring the tenant to remedy the breach`
    OR  a's `the lessor increases the rent payable under the residential tenancy agreement`
    OR  a's `the lessor takes action to terminate the residential tenancy agreement`
    OR  a's `at the end of the current residential tenancy agreement, the lessor refuses to enter into a further residential tenancy agreement with the tenant`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.26A
@export Decide whether the lessor takes retaliatory action against a tenant under s.26A
GIVEN a IS A `lessor action` @desc The lessor takes one of the s.26A(a) steps (breach-remedy notice other than rent, rent increase, action to terminate, or refusal of a further agreement) and is motivated wholly or partly by a s.26B(2) matter arising.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessor takes retaliatory action against the tenant` IF
        `the lessor takes action of a kind in section 26A(a)` a
    AND a's `the lessor is motivated to take the action, wholly or partly, by the matter arising`

§§§ `26B. Retaliatory action taken by lessor`

DECLARE `section 26B facts` HAS
    `the tenant reasonably believes the lessor took retaliatory action against the tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant or a representative entity asked for repairs or maintenance to the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant or a representative entity gave the lessor a notice claiming the lessor has breached the agreement and requiring the lessor to remedy the breach` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant or a representative entity required the lessor to reimburse the tenant for a reasonable expense properly incurred for urgent repairs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant or a representative entity applied to a competent court for an order under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor or lessor's agent knows that the tenant or a representative entity has complained to the Commissioner or another government entity about an act or omission of the lessor that adversely affected the tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an order of a competent court is in force in relation to the lessor and tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is satisfied the lessor's action was likely to have been retaliatory action for a matter mentioned in section 26B(2)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN f IS A `section 26B facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a matter mentioned in section 26B(2) arose` IF
        f's `the tenant or a representative entity asked for repairs or maintenance to the premises`
    OR  f's `the tenant or a representative entity gave the lessor a notice claiming the lessor has breached the agreement and requiring the lessor to remedy the breach`
    OR  f's `the tenant or a representative entity required the lessor to reimburse the tenant for a reasonable expense properly incurred for urgent repairs`
    OR  f's `the tenant or a representative entity applied to a competent court for an order under this Act`
    OR  f's `the lessor or lessor's agent knows that the tenant or a representative entity has complained to the Commissioner or another government entity about an act or omission of the lessor that adversely affected the tenant`
    OR  f's `an order of a competent court is in force in relation to the lessor and tenant`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.26B
@export Decide whether the tenant may apply for relief in relation to alleged retaliatory action under s.26B
GIVEN f IS A `section 26B facts` @desc The tenant reasonably believes the lessor took retaliatory action after a s.26B(2) matter: enforcement of tenant rights (repairs, breach notice, urgent-repair reimbursement, or court application), a complaint known to the lessor or agent, or a court order in force between them.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant may apply for relief in relation to alleged retaliatory action` IF
        f's `the tenant reasonably believes the lessor took retaliatory action against the tenant`
    AND `a matter mentioned in section 26B(2) arose` f

GIVEN f IS A `section 26B facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make an order in relation to retaliatory action` IF
        `the tenant may apply for relief in relation to alleged retaliatory action` f
    AND f's `the court is satisfied the lessor's action was likely to have been retaliatory action for a matter mentioned in section 26B(2)(a), (b) or (c)`

§§ `Fixtures`

`termination after repairs request` MEANS `lessor action` WITH
    `the lessor gives the tenant a notice claiming the tenant has breached the residential tenancy agreement, other than by failing to pay rent, and requiring the tenant to remedy the breach` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor increases the rent payable under the residential tenancy agreement` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor takes action to terminate the residential tenancy agreement` IS TRUE,
    `at the end of the current residential tenancy agreement, the lessor refuses to enter into a further residential tenancy agreement with the tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor is motivated to take the action, wholly or partly, by the matter arising` IS TRUE

`repairs then believed retaliation` MEANS `section 26B facts` WITH
    `the tenant reasonably believes the lessor took retaliatory action against the tenant` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant or a representative entity asked for repairs or maintenance to the premises` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant or a representative entity gave the lessor a notice claiming the lessor has breached the agreement and requiring the lessor to remedy the breach` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant or a representative entity required the lessor to reimburse the tenant for a reasonable expense properly incurred for urgent repairs` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant or a representative entity applied to a competent court for an order under this Act` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor or lessor's agent knows that the tenant or a representative entity has complained to the Commissioner or another government entity about an act or omission of the lessor that adversely affected the tenant` IS FALSE,
    `an order of a competent court is in force in relation to the lessor and tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the court is satisfied the lessor's action was likely to have been retaliatory action for a matter mentioned in section 26B(2)(a), (b) or (c)` IS TRUE

#EVAL `the lessor takes retaliatory action against the tenant` `termination after repairs request`
#EVAL `the tenant may apply for relief in relation to alleged retaliatory action` `repairs then believed retaliation`
#EVAL `the court may make an order in relation to retaliatory action` `repairs then believed retaliation`
#ASSERT `the lessor takes retaliatory action against the tenant` `termination after repairs request` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the tenant may apply for relief in relation to alleged retaliatory action` `repairs then believed retaliation` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the court may make an order in relation to retaliatory action` `repairs then believed retaliation` EQUALS TRUE
